{"name":"Artichoke","hex":"#8f9779","fetched":"2026-11-01","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"artichoke","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant related to the thistle with enlarged flower heads eaten as a vegetable while immature, Cynara cardunculus var. scolymus.","A dull green colour, like that of an artichoke."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/artichoke"}],"entries":[{"title":"Artichoke","blocks":[{"text":"The artichoke is a variety of a species of thistle cultivated as food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Artichoke_J1.jpg/330px-Artichoke_J1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artichoke","wikidata":"Q23041430"},{"title":"Artichoke (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Artichoke, also known as the Artichoke Trust, is a London-based British company and registered charitable trust that stages arts spectacles and live events. It was founded in 2005 by Helen Marriage, former director of the Salisbury International Arts Festival, and Nicky Webb."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/La_Princesse_on_move2.jpg/330px-La_Princesse_on_move2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artichoke_(company)","wikidata":"Q4800849"},{"title":"Shades of chartreuse","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of chartreuse are listed below. Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green, so named because of its resemblance to the color of the French liqueur green chartreuse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg/330px-Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_chartreuse","wikidata":"Q105563495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Artichoke_J1.jpg/500px-A